From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Lulejian <jlulejian@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:09:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/48] [Extensions] Validate frame activation in
 MessagePort::PostMessage

Previously, `MessagePort::PostMessage()` in the browser process
forwarded incoming `extensions::Message` structs from renderer processes
without verifying whether a sending `content::RenderFrameHost` actually
possessed browser-side transient user activation
(`frame->HasTransientUserActivation()`). A compromised frame renderer
(or a slow renderer that has exceeded the 5 second activation time)
could therefore send `user_gesture = true` over Mojo. This would cause
the receiving extension service worker or background page to synthesize
an active user gesture for the purposes of calling privileged chrome.*
APIs that require a user gesture.

With this change, `MessagePort::PostMessage()` verifies that any frame
sender claiming `user_gesture = true` has active transient user
activation (`frame->HasTransientUserActivation()`). If the frame is null
or lacks transient user activation, `user_gesture` is reset to `false`
before forwarding the message. We cannot kill the renderer because a
slow renderer could also find its way into this scenario if it exceeded
the 5 second user gesture activation time.

Fixed: 496187630
Change-Id: I6f97c86635ad4417599e622d22ce23b94562d539
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8415573
Commit-Queue: Justin Lulejian <jlulejian@chromium.org>
